.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH taur-gc 1  "taur-gc " 
.SH NAME
taur\-gc \- Prune unreachable Git objects older than the grace period
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtaur gc\fR [\fB\-\-grace\-secs\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prune unreachable Git objects older than the grace period.
.PP
A repository with a push quarantine or a lock file is skipped. This does not delete a package or a branch.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-grace\-secs\fR \fI<GRACE_SECS>\fR [default: 1209600]
Keep unreachable objects newer than this many seconds
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
Data directory (default: ~/.local/share/taur)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Command\-line flags take precedence over environment variables, which take precedence over defaults.
.TP
\fBTAUR_HOME\fR
Data directory (database, git repos, outbox, SSH host key). Default: ~/.local/share/taur.
